error[ffi_constant_type]: `CP_WIDE` in `fixedbugs-094-values.h` cannot be a `Cp`: clang refuses the header's value at line 17: implicit conversion from 'int' to 'char' changes value from 300 to 44
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-094-a-number-c-would-change-is-told.hero:14:5
     |
  14 |     constant CP_WIDE: Cp  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-094-values.h` line 17 reads `#define CP_WIDE {300, 2}`
  note: C only warns of this, and the accessor that builds a record's constant makes it an error: the value C would build is not the one the header wrote, or is of another kind than the field it fills
  note: a group's `constant` of a record is the value C builds when it initialises the header's `struct cp` with `CP_WIDE` (§ 13): declare it at the record whose value the header spells, or name the header that spells `CP_WIDE` for `struct cp`

